WEBVTT

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.120
Yotaka.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.800
Are you...

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.300
I'm... hungry.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.410
Clown Prescription
Score 5

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.220
Gareki-kun.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.720
Take Nai-chan and leave the village right away.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.310
Are you kidding?!

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.390
I need to talk to Yotaka!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.060
He's in no state to talk right now.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.520
Listen to me before you get yourself killed.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:00.660
He's moving.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.500
Let's meet up at Karasuna.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.790
I can't go with you, sorry.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.300
See you later.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:14.790
Damn it.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.050
What does he mean by "Listen to him"?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.340
Don't screw with me!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.420
I won't listen to you!

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.890
<i>They're my...</i>

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:29.310
If you don't have a name... How about "Gareki"? It means gravels of flower.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.400
How do you like it?

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.690
It's nice, isn't it?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.940
We're family.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.650
Nonsense. It's worthless.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.280
Here.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:42.450
What?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.080
Grandpa told me to bring you the scraps from the factory.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.410
You're... always fiddling with something.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.260
Hey, aren't you coming to dinner?

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.630
We're waiting for you Gareki.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:58.970
What?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.380
Are we supposed to eat meals together?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.440
There he is! I found Gareki!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.940
What do you want?

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.400
Want? Well...

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.080
I've been wondering where you were...

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.910
So, um...

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.910
Tsubame's been bugging me about where you've been, so...

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.250
Gareki.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.510
Why are you here?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.850
There's no way I could bring Tsubame to such a dangerous place, right?

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.270
So I was right.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:58.230
A gun? Why do you have such a thing?

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.900
What the hell have you been doing?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.780
It's none of your business.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.740
Answer me!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.120
Why are you still trying to act as if you're my brother?

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:16.090
How long do you think it's been since I left your place?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.220
You asked what I'm doing?

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:28.140
I'm doing the kind of things that would kill dorks like you and Tsubame if you got involved.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.510
Never come here again.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.100
You idiot.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.110
Go to hell!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.070
<i>Stay away from me.</i>

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.820
<i>Don't get involved with me.</i>

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:51.750
<i>I only deal with three kinds of people.</i>

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.090
<i>Scum, prey, and enemies.</i>

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.910
Hope you enjoy them.
from the field.
They're harvested

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.600
Are they stupid or something? Honestly...

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:14.060
Nai, go back by yourself.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.180
What?

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.730
This was the way we came.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.150
If you go straight, you'll return to Karasuna.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:21.610
Got it?

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.700
I'll lend this to you, so try not to stand out.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:27.450
No way!

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:29.320
I don't want to go! No!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.030
I don't want to go! No!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:30.790
Hey–

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.200
what's the matter?

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.410
That thing was scary.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:38.330
That's why I'm telling you to put on the hood and run away from here.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.540
That's not what I mean.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:43.090
I don't want Gareki to get broken up into pieces,

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.670
so I'll go with you!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:49.090
Hey... Stop saying such damned things.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.850
If there's anyone you should worry about, it should be
Yogi, who's gone to where Yotaka is, shouldn't it?

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.600
Yogi's strong.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.600
Then are you saying that I'm weak?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.400
You stupid animal!

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.570
What can you do if you come with me?!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.540
Listen, Nai.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.410
Your goal is to meet Karoku, isn't it?

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.840
You should remain calm and not get involved with unnecessary things like this.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:23.460
Make use of Circus to reach your goal.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:31.260
It's awkward to say this, but I'm feeling pretty frustrated.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:35.310
Seeing Yotaka transform in front of me.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:37.430
The same thing might happen to Tsubame.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:42.440
Yogi is probably intending to kill Yotaka.

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:47.730
But I have my reasons not to just stand around and do nothing.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.200
Even though I've cut my ties with them.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:58.450
They're the ones that I wish would always stay safe and sound.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.460
Gareki.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.800
Once you find an abandoned building,

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.510
go and hide yourself there!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.600
<i>You've got to be kidding.</i>

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:26.990
<i>A useless person like me and the one who ruined them should just go die!</i>

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:41.290
The "unnecessary things" that Gareki was talking about... What are they?

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.630
Something that has nothing to do with me?

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.420
That's not right.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.760
Gareki is going to where Tsubame-chan is.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.470
Even though what's happening to her has nothing to do with him.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:10.440
Again... I don't remember but people are dead.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.950
I must be sick after all.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:22.120
If something happened to me, Yotaka would be all alone.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.830
What should I do?

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.960
Are you okay?

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.180
Don't be afraid.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.480
Um, I...

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.390
Tsubame-chan!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.940
Ah.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.280
Blood...

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.030
<i>He hasn't completely transformed yet.</i>

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.440
<i>Maybe I can still...</i>

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.780
<i>Crate of Thorns!</i>

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.260
<i>Gather!</i>

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.240
Yotaka-kun, listen to me.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.070
I don't wish to fight you.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.030
Please...

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.540
For Gareki's sake too.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.580
Okay?

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:28.790
Gareki.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.970
Gare...ki.

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:08.830
Why?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.920
I don't... know.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.840
That man was scary.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.430
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.340
You've gotten blood on your hand...

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.930
I'm scary too, aren't I?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.440
Hm?

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.310
Being near me feels creepy, doesn't it?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.400
No...

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.230
What?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.350
You feel warm.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.070
<i>She's so warm... just like Karoku.</i>

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.330
Tsubame-chan, you're warm and pretty.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.160
That's why Gareki said...

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.370
What?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.370
He wanted you to always be safe and sound.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.590
I've always thought he hated me.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:05.640
That's not true! Well, ah, um...

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:07.520
Thank you.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.390
Nai-chan, you're kind too.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.140
Isn’t that nice?

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.070
Young people really make me smile.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:52.850
This guy...

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.560
He had no intention of killing me.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:58.810
Why?

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:05.190
Who is this guy?

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.360
Yotaka!

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.370
Yotaka, you..

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:13.790
What's wrong with you?

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.790
What happened...

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:23.010
It's so much more fun to have more people around.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:26.510
This will bring my research that much closer to completion.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:29.760
Yogi...

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.390
Oh yeah, let's have a party to celebrate our encounter.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:38.650
Let's have lots of fun!

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:41.400
Tonight's menu will be... this!

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.210
Yotaka...

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.590
Gareki...

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.720
What's up with that look?

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.970
What the hell are you doing?

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:18.480
It has nothing to do with you, right?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:26.150
Those were your words back then...

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.160
You...

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:32.120
What are you going to do with Tsubame and your grandfather?

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.950
Shut up.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.960
It's too late.

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.620
I'll kill you.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.290
You fool.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.880
Wonderful.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.380
Young people are so passionate.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.890
Who the hell are you?

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.020
Even if you ask me who I am...

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:58.020
I'm just someone from somewhere.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.390
I like games where I can nurture characters, and I'm playing one right now...

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.650
I wanted to retrieve the data on both the twins,

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:12.160
but Yotaka became suspicious of the drug.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:15.200
He took Tsubame's dosage as well,

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:19.210
so even if Tsubame resonated, she didn't transform.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:24.590
He even continued to take the drug,
in order to get money for the experiment.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.420
He's so devoted to his family.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.380
Yotaka!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.640
You bastard.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:33.880
I see... So you're the one...

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.270
Tsubaki was also...

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:40.890
Oh yes.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.390
I think she was trying to save her little brother.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:50.240
When Yotaka transformed for the first time, his power went berserk.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:54.330
She jumped in, even though she didn't understand what was going on.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:55.950
And so she...

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.620
That's why, I wasn't the one who killed her.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.500
I wanted to make love to her a little more.

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:13.140
You're the one who killed her!

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:15.220
Open your mind and think clearly!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.850
I've seen your face before.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:20.850
What?

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:25.520
Let me draw flightless wings on your back as well, someday.

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:27.570
Or...

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:28.900
Varuga!

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.240
Do you want me to do it now, human?!

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.210
I thought you were dead.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.960
How disappointing.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:56.680
Yotaka, I command you...

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.680
to kill everyone here.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.520
No, you mustn't!

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.150
Yotaka won't do it!

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.020
He won't do such a thing!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.190
I won't do it.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.530
I won't kill.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.120
I refuse to do it!

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:32.550
Oh, I see. So, that's how it is.

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:36.010
So there was a reverse resonance between the two of them, as well.

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:41.260
I've been wondering why he was able to cling onto his last shred of humanity.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:45.650
I guess that's due to Tsubame pulling him back to his original self.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:49.820
I see... So this only happens with twins, huh?

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.020
Interesting.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:58.910
But I'm curious, what's so great about living a life of poverty?

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.950
"What"?

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:03.500
You don't even know that?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:11.580
If you can't figure out what it means to laugh and cry each passing day,

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.800
then I feel sorry for you.

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:22.220
That’s enough.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.810
I've lost interest.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.980
But I'll tell you something.

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:30.810
You can never return to the past.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.570
You cannot resist your transformation.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:41.240
Yotaka!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.240
Trying to resist... What a futile effort.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.210
Don't get in the way.

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.760
I'm just getting to the best part now.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:00.840
No!

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.890
Gareki...

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.020
Kill me.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.520
Gareki...

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:29.670
I don't want to hurt anyone... anymore!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:34.000
Please, Gareki...

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:36.460
I'm begging you, kill me...

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:41.260
Gareki!
Gareki!
Gareki!

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:15.090
Tsubame...

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.050
Yotaka?

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:34.560
Tsubame,

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:38.360
fly somewhere...

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.860
far away...

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:47.700
Yotaka!

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.420
Smells nice, doesn't it?

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:29.050
That's a flower.

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.590
Its fragrance smells nice...

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:31.800
Is it something to eat?

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:34.220
No, it's something to admire.

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:35.890
Karoku also smells good.

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:36.890
What?

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:38.520
You smell just like the sun.
